{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Notice that we were asked to find the one-sided limit, $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -4^+}f(x)$. This is the limit where $x$-values approach $-4$ from the right.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's find the limit as $x$ approaches $-4$ from the right. We will use the fact that $f(x)=2^x$ for $x$-values greater than $-4$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -4^+}f(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -4^+}2^x\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2^{-4}\u0026\\gray{\\text{Direct substitution}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{16}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, we found that $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -4^+}f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{16}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$f(x)=\\begin{cases}\n\\dfrac{1}{x+1}\u0026\\text{for }-5\u003cx\\leq -4\n\\\\\\\\\n2^x\u0026\\text{for }x\u003e-4\n\\end{cases}$\n\n**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -4^+}f(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-4$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac13$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{16}$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
